{"id": "SGU_Episode_315", "title": "SGU Episode 315", "type": "structured", "description": "The Skeptic's Guide to the Universe, Episode 315 Transcript", "metadata": {"title": "SGU Episode 315", "date": "July 27 2024", "year": 2024, "month": 7, "day": 27, "rogues": ["Rebecca Watson", "Steven Novella", "Jay Novella", "Evan Bernstein", "Bob Novella"], "quotee_url": "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dr._Manhattan", "quote": "\n 'A live body and a dead body contain the same number of particles. Structurally, there\u2019s no discernible difference. Life and death are unquantifiable abstracts. Why should I be concerned?' \n", "quotee": "\n Dr. Manhattan \n", "quotee_title": "", "categories": [], "podcast_url": "https://www.theskepticsguide.org/podcasts/episode-315", "episode_number": 315}, "sections": [{"id": 0, "text": "You're listening to the Skeptics' Guide to the Universe, your escape to reality.\n", "title": "Introduction", "metadata": {"title": "Introduction"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 1, "text": "July 30, 1898,: Corn Flakes were invented by William Kellogg.", "title": "This Day in Skepticism", "metadata": {"timestamp": "", "hour": 0, "minute": 0, "second": 0, "title": "This Day in Skepticism"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 2, "text": "", "title": "News Items", "metadata": {"timestamp": "", "hour": 0, "minute": 0, "second": 0, "title": "News Items"}, "sections": [{"id": 3, "text": "http://www.theskepticsguide.org/resources/events.aspx", "title": "TAM9 and Upcoming Events", "metadata": {"timestamp": "", "hour": 0, "minute": 0, "second": 0, "links": ["http://www.theskepticsguide.org/resources/events.aspx"], "title": "TAM9 and Upcoming Events"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 4, "text": "http://ncse.com/news/2011/07/victory-evolution-texas-006802", "title": "Victory for Evolution in Texas", "metadata": {"timestamp": "", "hour": 0, "minute": 0, "second": 0, "links": ["http://ncse.com/news/2011/07/victory-evolution-texas-006802"], "title": "Victory for Evolution in Texas"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 5, "text": "http://www.bbc.co.uk/news/science-environment-14220620", "title": "New Moon for Pluto", "metadata": {"timestamp": "", "hour": 0, "minute": 0, "second": 0, "links": ["http://www.bbc.co.uk/news/science-environment-14220620"], "title": "New Moon for Pluto"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 6, "text": "http://www.space.com/12421-alien-life-rare-universe-extraterrestrials-seti.html", "title": "Life in the Universe", "metadata": {"timestamp": "", "hour": 0, "minute": 0, "second": 0, "links": ["http://www.space.com/12421-alien-life-rare-universe-extraterrestrials-seti.html"], "title": "Life in the Universe"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 7, "text": "http://fairfield.patch.com/articles/southport-resident-reports-sighting-of-bizarre-creature-some-claim-is-a-chupacabra#photo-752971", "title": "Connecticut Chupacabra", "metadata": {"timestamp": "", "hour": 0, "minute": 0, "second": 0, "links": ["http://fairfield.patch.com/articles/southport-resident-reports-sighting-of-bizarre-creature-some-claim-is-a-chupacabra#photo-752971"], "title": "Connecticut Chupacabra"}, "sections": []}]}, {"id": 8, "text": "Answer to last week: Barn Owl", "title": "Who's That Noisy", "metadata": {"timestamp": "", "hour": 0, "minute": 0, "second": 0, "title": "Who's That Noisy"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 9, "text": "http://planetary.org/home/", "title": "Interview with Bill Nye", "metadata": {"timestamp": "", "hour": 0, "minute": 0, "second": 0, "links": ["http://planetary.org/home/"], "title": "Interview with Bill Nye"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 10, "text": "Item #1: A new analysis indicates that the greatest threat to endangered large African mammal species is the conservation laws designed to protect them.\nItem #2: Biologists discover that the cottony cushion scale insect fertilizes its eggs with sperm that live inside of it as a separate infectious tissue lineage.\nItem #3: Scientists discover that the biomass of a species in a given ecosystem is determined entirely by it's place in the food chain, and not by animal type, size, or other variable.\n", "title": "Science or Fiction", "metadata": {"timestamp": "", "hour": 0, "minute": 0, "second": 0, "title": "Science or Fiction"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 11, "text": "", "title": "Skeptical Quote of the Week", "metadata": {"timestamp": "", "hour": 0, "minute": 0, "second": 0, "title": "Skeptical Quote of the Week"}, "sections": [{"id": 12, "text": "'A live body and a dead body contain the same number of particles. Structurally, there\u2019s no discernible difference. Life and death are unquantifiable abstracts. Why should I be concerned?' - Dr. Manhattan", "metadata": {"speaker": "<unknown>"}}]}, {"id": 13, "text": "", "title": "References", "metadata": {"title": "References"}, "sections": []}]}